  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="Samuel Pepys">
      <data key="d0">Samuel Pepys</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The author and main narrator of the diary; identified in the title as M.A., F.R.S., Clerk of the Acts, and Secretary to the Admiralty. The entry records activities on June 1 and 2, 1661.&lt;SEP&gt;The diarist and narrator of the passage; practises singing, dines with My Lady, works at the office, visits Moorefields and Deptford, meets friends at the Bell, sleeps in the Nursery, and attends church.&lt;SEP&gt;Diarist who records his daily activities in July 1661, including household purchases, music practice, household concerns, and reporting to the Duke of York about the ships.&lt;SEP&gt;The diary writer and first-person narrator of the passage, who visits the Theatre, hears news of Robert Pepys, travels to Brampton, and records the surrounding events.&lt;SEP&gt;English diarist and central figure of the passage; records his travels, meetings, social visits, theatre attendance, borrowed money, and family interactions in July–August 1661.&lt;SEP&gt;Diarist and author of the diary; the narrator whose observations and actions are described in the text.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-050</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445818</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Diary of Samuel Pepys">
      <data key="d0">Diary of Samuel Pepys</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The diary written by Samuel Pepys, covering in this section the entries for June, July, and August 1661. The text is transcribed from a shorthand manuscript and includes notes and editorial additions.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445818</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
