    <node id="Lady Batten">
      <data key="d0">Lady Batten</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Person referred to as “my Lady” in the text; she left with Sir W. Batten to keep Whitsuntide.&lt;SEP&gt;Wife of Sir W. Batten; reported out of town and therefore absent from the Sunday dinner.&lt;SEP&gt;A woman who traveled in a two-coach party with The Diarist to see Bartholomew Fayre.&lt;SEP&gt;Woman referred to as my Lady Batten; she was the subject of gossip that she had been the mistress of a man who left her his estate.&lt;SEP&gt;A woman who spent the afternoon at the Theatre with Sir W. Pen.&lt;SEP&gt;Lady mentioned in the same passage as the King, Duke, Duchess, and Madame Palmer.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-050</data>
