    <node id="Narrator's House">
      <data key="d0">Narrator's House</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Narrator's house, where he dined with his father, Cousin Scott, and others, where the Bowyer party stayed all afternoon, and where he later walked with his wife.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator's residence where goods are brought and stored overnight and where painters work on the stairs.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator's home, which was being cleaned and which the narrator found very clean on the 21st and 22nd.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator's home, shown to Lady Jem and Pall; their mother had previously come alone with the Narrator's Wife to inspect it.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator's dwelling where he gave fruit and wine to Lord Hinchingbroke on Saturday.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator's home, used as a place where My Lady sends her sons.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-036</data>
