    <node id="Mr. Moore">
      <data key="d0">Mr. Moore</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mr. Moore is an acquaintance, advisor, and close companion of the diarist Samuel Pepys, appearing frequently in Pepys’s personal and professional activities. Lord Sandwich (referred to as “My Lord”) intended to join Mr. Moore with Pepys in managing Wardrobe business during his absence. Mr. Moore was a companion at the Wardrobe, where Pepys shared a bed with him in Mr. Moore’s chamber. He also accompanied Pepys on numerous excursions, including to Westminster Hall, the Theatre (leaving from Pepys’s mother’s house), Fenchurch Street, and into the City, where they parted. On other occasions, Mr. Moore and Pepys hired a coach together to Chelsea to examine and seal a document with the Lord Privy Seal, drank together at a tavern near the Savoy and at the Mitre, and met at My Lady’s house before dining at the Wardrobe, where Mr. Moore informed Pepys that the next day was a Seal day.

Professionally, Mr. Moore acted as an advisor. At Pepys’s request, he sent advice that the three witnesses of a will being legatees would not invalidate the will. Pepys found him at home on one occasion, where Mr. Moore dined with Pepys and read his uncle’s will, offering an opinion on it. After Pepys’s deputation was accepted, Mr. Moore read over all the bills at White Hall. At Whitehall, he also told Pepys that Lady Sandwich had given birth to a daughter. Additionally, Mr. Moore gave Pepys a copy of Hooker’s Ecclesiastical Polity, which had been given the previous Wednesday. Through these varied interactions, Mr. Moore emerges as a trusted and frequent associate of Pepys in both business and social matters.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-048</data>
