    </node>
    <node id="Lord Chancellor">
      <data key="d0">Lord Chancellor</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Official from whom the Narrator receives orders during My Lord's absence.&lt;SEP&gt;Lord Chancellor is a high official who is envied and undermined by the Duke of Buckingham and the Lord of Bristoll; the King relies on the Lord Chancellor for policy and service.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445848</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mr. Edward Montagu">
      <data key="d0">Mr. Edward Montagu</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Person from whom the Narrator receives orders during My Lord's absence as to the great preparation.&lt;SEP&gt;A man found by the narrator at My Lord's Whitehall residence; he comes with his family to stay during My Lord's absence.&lt;SEP&gt;Man in Westminster visited by the diarist about business concerning My Lord.&lt;SEP&gt;Man disposing of L5000 for Lord Sandwich's departure; the narrator and Lady Sandwich feared Mr Edward Montagu would not act to Lord Sandwich's honour or profit.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-045</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445848</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Trinity House">
      <data key="d0">Trinity House</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Organization that chooses a Master; My Lord is chosen Master of Trinity House and dines there on that day.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-006</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445848</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Office">
      <data key="d0">Office</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative office at which the Narrator works and where Sir G. Carteret joins the Narrator. The Office has no money, its credit is low, and sellers will not supply without personal security.&lt;SEP&gt;A place the narrator goes to after visiting the painters.&lt;SEP&gt;A workplace where the Diarist spent the whole afternoon and enjoyed talking with persons of quality and being in command.&lt;SEP&gt;The office where the Narrator and colleagues are; quiet but lacking money, with bills sold at a loss and a plan to add a house.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-049</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445848</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sir G. Carteret">
      <data key="d0">Sir G. Carteret</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Person at the Office with the Narrator; Sir G. Carteret agrees with the Narrator on a letter to the Duke of York about the Office's lack of money.&lt;SEP&gt;A man who had invited some officers to dinner at Deptford but did not send for the narrator to go with them.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-033</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445848</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Duke of York">
      <data key="d0">Duke of York</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Person to whom a letter from the Office is to be sent describing the Office's need for money.&lt;SEP&gt;Royal person who sent an order to Samuel Pepys to give an account of why the ships had not been sent out and who received the account at Whitehall.&lt;SEP&gt;A person whom the Narrator, Sir W. Batten, and Sir W. Pen wait upon to give an account of the Navy's condition.&lt;SEP&gt;The royal duke who receives an account of the Navy's lack of money and says he will speak to the King and Council about it.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-037</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445848</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Walden">
      <data key="d0">Walden</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Parliament-man for Huntingdon and companion of the Narrator on the outing to drink Lambeth ale.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-006</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445848</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rolt">
      <data key="d0">Rolt</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Companion of the Narrator on the outing to drink Lambeth ale.</data>
