    <node id="Huntingdon">
      <data key="d0">Huntingdon</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Town and parliamentary constituency that Walden serves as Parliament-man.&lt;SEP&gt;Huntingdon is a town to which the narrator travels to meet Sir Robert Bernard, where several social and business meetings take place.&lt;SEP&gt;A town where the Assizes also begin.&lt;SEP&gt;Town mentioned together with Cambridge at the beginning of the passage in connection with Samuel Pepys's journey to meet Roger Pepys.&lt;SEP&gt;A town that The Narrator rides to; The Narrator waits there, later returns, and drinks there with Thomas Trice and Mr. Phillips.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-031</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445848</data>
      <data key="d6" />
