    <node id="Whitehall">
      <data key="d0">Whitehall</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Whitehall is a royal and governmental precinct in London, closely associated with the court and official business. It appears as the site of My Lord’s house or residence, where the diarist or narrator sought My Lord, and also as a place the narrator went to and later met My Lord. Access was often by water: Whitehall was the destination of My Lord’s barge, and the narrator and his wife travelled there by water; on another occasion the narrator went with My Lord by barge, and My Lord took leave of the King at Whitehall. At that royal location, the Duke of York, the King, and the Portuguese Ambassador were present.

In the diary’s itinerary, Whitehall fits between the Wardrobe and Westminster: the narrator visited it on the 5th after going to the Wardrobe and before proceeding to Westminster. While at Whitehall, the diarist walked about, met Mr. Pierce and Dean Fuller, and was joined by W. Howe. He also went there early one morning, but the Lord Privy Seal did not come that morning. On the 15th, Whitehall was a royal and government location where the diarist walked about. On another visit, the narrator stayed at Whitehall until past three o’clock, and while there Mr. Moore gave him news of Lady Sandwich. Thus, Whitehall serves in the account as both a court and government setting for official encounters and as a place connected to My Lord’s residence, personal meetings, and the exchange of news.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-041</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
