    <node id="A Form of Prayer">
      <data key="d0">A Form of Prayer</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A prayer document published for use in London on the 12th and in the country on the 19th of June; set forth by His Majesty's authority; it contained prayers against sicknesses, dearth, and scarcity, thanksgiving for fair weather, and a blessing on Parliament.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-007</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445853</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="General Fast">
      <data key="d0">General Fast</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A special appointed fasting day on 12 and 19 June to avert feared sicknesses, dearth, and scarcity after immoderate rain and waters, and to give thanks for the blessed change of weather.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-007</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445853</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="The Office">
      <data key="d0">The Office</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Office was the workplace of the diarist/Narrator, Samuel Pepys, where he went to sit and do business. He attended The Office at various times of day: after dinner in the evening, during the afternoon after visits, at the beginning of the day, and for whole mornings, including the whole morning on the 31st and again on August 2nd. On one occasion he was called there while guests were present and stayed only briefly before returning home. On another, he went there after coming home by water and remained until night after dining. He also spent an afternoon there in command, talking with people of quality.

The Office was a place where he and his colleagues resumed morning sittings and conducted business, sometimes meeting there about the business of Tangier. A particular route shows him going to The Office after Duck Lane and before going to Sir W. Batten’s house. Sir R. Ford’s house was added, or might be added, as additional quarters for The Office. While at The Office one morning, news of a dying man was brought to him, and he returned there after visiting the man. On another occasion, he spent the morning there while the office clerks attended Tom Whitton’s burial.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-042</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445855</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
