    <node id="The Theatre">
      <data key="d0">The Theatre</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Theatre is a playhouse attended by the diarist Samuel Pepys and his associates. It staged a variety of plays, including *Harry the 4th*, *The Alchymist*, *Claracilla*, *Brenoralt*, *The Jovial Crew* (also written as “The Joviall Crew”), and *Antipodes*. Pepys visited on several occasions, sometimes in the afternoon, and once carried his own party to see a performance there. He saw *Claracilla* in the afternoon of the 4th and noted that the theatre had become empty since the Opera began. He also watched *Brenoralt* while sitting before Mrs. Palmer, and met Mr. Bostock when seeing *Antipodes*.

Other attendees included Sir W. Pen and My Lady Batten, who were present for a performance of *The Alchymist* and also at an afternoon visit. Mr. Moore accompanied Pepys to see *The Jovial Crew*, at which the royal party was present. The theatre thus served not only as a venue for dramatic performances, but as a regular site of social engagement among Pepys’s circle.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-046</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445859</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
