    <node id="Westminster">
      <data key="d0">Westminster</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Westminster, a location in London, appears in the diary of Samuel Pepys as both a site of business and social activity. Pepys visited Westminster on multiple occasions to conduct several items of business, including once before dining at the Wardrobe and again on the 23rd after visiting Sir W. Pen and Batten. It was the location of Mr. Montagu’s chamber. The diarist also went to Westminster by accompanying Mr. Ch. Carter before the two parted ways.

Westminster was also a setting for social encounters and travel. Pepys went there to dine with the Lord, who had lodgings in the area, and with Ned Dickering. He walked to Westminster together with Mr. Marsh and Mr. Marsh’s wife. Westminster was accessible from Whitehall via a passage; the narrator traveled from Whitehall to Westminster at the end of that passage. Additionally, Westminster lay on the river, where Captain Bun landed some of the boat’s passengers.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-040</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445863</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
