    <node id="Roger Pepys">
      <data key="d0">Roger Pepys</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Cousin of the diarist; met the diarist in Westminster Hall while going to the Parliament House.&lt;SEP&gt;Son of Talbot Pepys, who succeeded his father as Recorder of Cambridge in 1660 according to the editorial note.&lt;SEP&gt;The person The Narrator intends to meet for counsel in connection with the Assizes at Cambridge and Huntingdon.&lt;SEP&gt;Person whom Samuel Pepys intended to meet for counsel before setting out on horseback toward Cambridge.&lt;SEP&gt;A cousin of the narrator whom the narrator consults about the uncle's will; he rides with the narrator to Impington and is regarded as a sober, honorable man.&lt;SEP&gt;A sober relative of The Narrator with whom The Narrator discusses public matters; Roger Pepys criticizes the young men in Parliament and fears that they may cause another war.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-031</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
