    <node id="Diarist's Mother">
      <data key="d0">Diarist's Mother</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mother of the Diarist; visited by the Diarist, and believes a large fortune has fallen to her.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Aunt Bell">
      <data key="d0">Aunt Bell</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An aunt of the Diarist; present at the Diarist's mother's house and involved in the women's talk.&lt;SEP&gt;An aunt of the Narrator; comes to the Narrator's house for the first time to dine, then visits Aunt Wight.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-046</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mrs. Ramsey">
      <data key="d0">Mrs. Ramsey</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A woman present at the Diarist's mother's house, taking part in the conversation with the older women.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mr. Hill of Cambridge">
      <data key="d0">Mr. Hill of Cambridge</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A man met at Pope's Head Alley; spoke about state affairs and told the Diarist that the King would be forced to favour Presbytery.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pope's Head Alley">
      <data key="d0">Pope's Head Alley</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A place where the Diarist met Mr. Hill of Cambridge and women, and went into a tavern.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="England">
      <data key="d0">England</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The country whose whole state, regarding the Church, Mr. Hill claimed had changed the previous day.&lt;SEP&gt;England is the country whose state as to the Church is mentioned at the outset.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="The City">
      <data key="d0">The City</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The city mentioned in Mr. Hill's political talk, which would leave the King if the King did not favour Presbytery.&lt;SEP&gt;The City denotes the political body of London that would abandon the King if Presbytery were not favoured.&lt;SEP&gt;The district of London to which Mr. Moore and The Narrator walk before parting.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-028</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Presbytery">
      <data key="d0">Presbytery</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Presbyterian form of church government; according to Mr. Hill, the King would be forced to favour it.&lt;SEP&gt;Presbytery is a system of church government; the King would be forced to favour Presbytery, otherwise the City would leave the King.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Parliament">
      <data key="d0">Parliament</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The English Parliament; the Diarist, on inquiry, found that things there had changed.&lt;SEP&gt;Parliament is the English legislative body; Parliament is in disorder and its expected adjournment for two or three months was hindered for a day or two.&lt;SEP&gt;The legislative body that The King is expected to come and adjourn.&lt;SEP&gt;The legislative assembly in which public matters are described as being carried by young men.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-031</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="The Church">
      <data key="d0">The Church</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The church whose state in England had changed on the previous day, according to Mr. Hill.&lt;SEP&gt;The church that the Narrator and his Wife attended on the Sunday, together with Mrs. Ramsay in the morning and again in the afternoon.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-027</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="The Jovial Crew">
      <data key="d0">The Jovial Crew</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A play seen by the Diarist at the Theatre; described as merry, innocent, and well performed.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Diarist's Journal">
      <data key="d0">Diarist's Journal</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The written diary entries set down by the Diarist at night, covering the time since leaving London.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Papers of the Diarist's Uncle">
      <data key="d0">Papers of the Diarist's Uncle</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Papers belonging to the Diarist's uncle that arrived by box from Brampton and gave the Diarist work.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tavern at Pope's Head Alley">
      <data key="d0">Tavern at Pope's Head Alley</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A tavern in Pope's Head Alley where Mr. Hill of Cambridge brought the Diarist and some women and gave them wine.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Will's Clock">
      <data key="d0">Will's Clock</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A clock belonging to the Diarist's servant Will; Will lost it together with the Diarist's tankard.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Diarist's Tankard">
      <data key="d0">Diarist's Tankard</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A tankard belonging to the Diarist; Will lost it together with Will's clock.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Diarist's Deceased Uncle">
      <data key="d0">Diarist's Deceased Uncle</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Diarist's late uncle whose papers were sent in a box from Brampton and whose inheritance is connected to the estate left to the Diarist.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-025</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="King">
      <data key="d0">King</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The King is the monarch of England discussed in the account; the King would be forced to favour Presbytery to keep the City from leaving, and cannot do without the Lord Chancellor for policy and service.&lt;SEP&gt;Monarch mentioned in the passage. The King gives a handwritten warrant to the Chancellor, appears at Worcester House in a plain riding-suit and velvet cap, and receives money voted by the Parliament of Ireland.&lt;SEP&gt;Monarch mentioned alongside the Duke and Duchess; Mrs. Palmer is described as the King's mistress.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-050</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Church">
      <data key="d0">Church</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Church is the religious institution whose state in England is the opening concern of the passage.&lt;SEP&gt;The church to which the narrator went after leaving the alehouse, where the narrator stayed through the sermon while the narrator's father's family appeared in mourning.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-042</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="God">
      <data key="d0">God</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">God is the deity from whom the Narrator hopes to receive forgiveness for breaking a vow to drink no wine.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mr. Montagu">
      <data key="d0">Mr. Montagu</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mr. Montagu is the person in whose chamber at Westminster the Narrator heard a Frenchman play the guitar.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Frenchman">
      <data key="d0">Frenchman</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Frenchman is a friend of Monsieur Eschar who played the guitar extremely well in Mr. Montagu's chamber.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Monsieur Eschar">
      <data key="d0">Monsieur Eschar</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Monsieur Eschar is the person whose friend the Frenchman is.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Guitar">
      <data key="d0">Guitar</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Guitar is the instrument played by the Frenchman in Mr. Montagu's chamber.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mr. George Montagu">
      <data key="d0">Mr. George Montagu</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mr. George Montagu is a man spoken to by the Narrator in the lobby of Westminster Hall; Mr. George Montagu discussed the ship for Lord Hinchingbroke and reported the political situation involving the Lord Chancellor.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lord Hinchingbroke">
      <data key="d0">Lord Hinchingbroke</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Lord Hinchingbroke is a young lord who, with the other young gentlemen, resolved to go to France in a hired vessel from Rye rather than in a man of war.&lt;SEP&gt;A lord who became ill after the narrator gave him fruit and wine; was in great fear of smallpox.&lt;SEP&gt;A nobleman staying at My Lady's house who is recovering from illness and is found by the diarist to be gradually better.&lt;SEP&gt;A nobleman recovering from illness; sits up and walks about the chamber.&lt;SEP&gt;A lord from whom the narrator took leave at the Wardrobe; Lord Hinchingbroke rode with the brother toward Rye on the way to France.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-045</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rye">
      <data key="d0">Rye</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Rye is the port from which Lord Hinchingbroke and the young gentlemen resolved to sail.&lt;SEP&gt;The town toward which Lord Hinchingbroke and the brother travelled by coach before reaching France.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-045</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Duke Of Buckingham">
      <data key="d0">Duke Of Buckingham</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Duke Of Buckingham is a great man who, according to Mr. George Montagu, endeavours to undermine the Lord Chancellor.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lord Of Bristoll">
      <data key="d0">Lord Of Bristoll</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Lord Of Bristoll is a nobleman who, with the Duke of Buckingham, endeavours to undermine the Lord Chancellor.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lord Of Sandwich">
      <data key="d0">Lord Of Sandwich</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Lord Of Sandwich is the nobleman whose birthday was celebrated at the Wardrobe with many friends.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Captain Isham">
      <data key="d0">Captain Isham</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Captain Isham is a person who was among the friends at the Wardrobe for Lord of Sandwich's birthday.&lt;SEP&gt;A captain who was part of the merry company with Mr. Townsend and shared the venison pasty.&lt;SEP&gt;An acquaintance of the narrator going with Mr Fanshaw toward Portugal.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-045</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mr. Pargiter">
      <data key="d0">Mr. Pargiter</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mr. Pargiter is a merchant who was also at the Wardrobe gathering.&lt;SEP&gt;A merchant who was also with the Narrator's company on the day of the dinner.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-027</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mr. Townsend's Wife">
      <data key="d0">Mr. Townsend's Wife</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mr. Townsend's Wife is the unnamed wife of Mr. Townsend who was among the friends gathered at the Wardrobe for Lord Of Sandwich's birthday.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Captain Ferrers' Lady">
      <data key="d0">Captain Ferrers' Lady</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The wife or companion of Captain Ferrers; included in the same merry dinner company as Mr. Townsend and others.&lt;SEP&gt;Captain Ferrers' Lady is the unnamed lady associated with Captain Ferrers and was among the friends gathered at the Wardrobe.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-027</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lord Of Sandwich's Birthday">
      <data key="d0">Lord Of Sandwich's Birthday</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Lord Of Sandwich's Birthday is the occasion being celebrated at the Wardrobe, attended by the Narrator, his wife, and many friends.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="The Narrator's Vow To Drink No Wine">
      <data key="d0">The Narrator's Vow To Drink No Wine</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A vow made by The Narrator at the beginning of the week to drink no wine for that week; The Narrator broke the vow on the day described and hoped God would forgive the breaking of it.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Townsend's Wife">
      <data key="d0">Townsend's Wife</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The wife of Mr. Townsend; part of the merry dinner party that ate venison pasty.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-027</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Captain Cooke">
      <data key="d0">Captain Cooke</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A captain who called on Mr. Townsend after dinner, joined the Narrator and Mr. Townsend at a tavern, and sang in what the Narrator considered the best manner in the world.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-027</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lady Jem">
      <data key="d0">Lady Jem</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A young woman who, with Pall, was taken by water through the bridge by the Narrator and his wife to see ships and the Narrator's house.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-027</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lady Jem and Pall's Mother">
      <data key="d0">Lady Jem and Pall's Mother</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The mother of Lady Jem and Pall, referred to as "my Lady"; had recently gone alone with the Narrator's Wife to look at the Narrator's house while the Narrator was away.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-027</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788445866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mrs. Ramsay">
      <data key="d0">Mrs. Ramsay</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A visitor who came to see the Narrator and his Wife on a Sunday, went to church, and dined with them.</data>
