    <node id="Lord Sandwich">
      <data key="d0">Lord Sandwich</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A nobleman referred to as "My Lord" and "my Lord of Sandwich"; the narrator is sworn as Lord Sandwich's deputy, and Lord Sandwich's preparations for Portugal require a 5,000-pound warrant.&lt;SEP&gt;A lord confirmed to be sick ashore at Alicante; the narrator fears for his family if he should die.&lt;SEP&gt;The man referred to in the text as "my Lord"; the vessel sent by the narrator carried Lord Sandwich's things toward Lynn.&lt;SEP&gt;A lord recovering from fever; Lord Sandwich lay sick at Alicante, was twice bled, sent a letter to the narrator, and had money arranged for a departure to Portugal.&lt;SEP&gt;A lord who is in the Straits and has recently recovered from a serious sickness at Alicante.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-048</data>
