    <edge source="Narrator" target="Narrator's Father">
      <data key="d7">15.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Narrator's Father is the father of the Narrator, making the Narrator a son of a man who owns the family trade. The Narrator demonstrated concern for his father's finances, wishing to spend some of his own means to help him, which led him to choose Mr. Young's place. He also wrote a letter to his father at Brampton and was troubled at not having heard back since leaving him.

The two had numerous personal encounters. The Narrator's Father dined at the Narrator's house with Cousin Scott; on another occasion he came to the Narrator's home and announced his intention to go into the country the next day. The Narrator went to his father's house, and later the father went with him to the Bear Tavern, an alehouse. They also met by appointment at Uncle Fenner's house. After the theatre, the Narrator and his wife went to the Narrator's Father's house and stayed to talk for a while.

In practical matters, the Narrator and his father together decided on scarlet, purple, and black cloth as well as £50 in linen. The Narrator argued with his father over Pall and, after bringing down Pall's high spirit, got his father to yield. He also obtained his father's consent for Pall to go into the country with the Narrator's mother and father, to see how Pall would behave. Additionally, together with Tom, the Narrator and his father set matters even and cast up the father's accounts, reflecting their shared involvement in financial and domestic affairs.</data>
      <data key="d9">accompanied,accounts,argued,arrangement,consent,consulted,corresponded_with,decided,dined with,family relation,father of,informed,meets at Uncle Fenner's,persuaded,settlement,son of,visited,visits,wished to provide for,wrote_to</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-049</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1788445913</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Narrator" target="My Lord">
      <data key="d7">11.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relation between My Lord and the Narrator is one of patronage, trust, and delegated responsibility, centered on the business of the Wardrobe. Before going to sea, My Lord instructed the Narrator in Wardrobe affairs and told him he placed great confidence in him. My Lord also said that the Narrator was to go to Mr. Townsend to learn the mystery of the Wardrobe, and he intended to make the Narrator deputy with Mr. Townsend, given the possibility that Mr. Townsend might die during My Lord’s absence.

The Narrator, in turn, sought and received preferment. He asked My Lord for the refusal of Mr. Young’s place in the Wardrobe should it fall, and My Lord freely promised him the refusal. The Narrator went to My Lord’s residence at Whitehall; on his second visit, he found and spoke with My Lord. On another occasion, by My Lord’s order, My Lord’s triangle virginall was sent to the Narrator’s own house. When My Lord was absent, he sent for the Narrator and entrusted him with seeing all things done concerning the great preparation. The Narrator also spoke at the Tower for ammunition for ships that were for My Lord, wrote to My Lord to report what had been done about the goods, and had letters for My Lord that were not ready when Captain Isham called for them.</data>
      <data key="d9">carries out order,entrusts,informed,instructed,letters,make deputy,not ready,oversight,promised,requested,requested supplies for,served,sought,told,trusted,visits residence,went to see,will appoint,wrote to</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-043</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1788445925</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Narrator" target="Mr. Moore">
      <data key="d7">1.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Mr. Moore was to be joined with the Narrator in the Wardrobe business under My Lord's arrangement.</data>
      <data key="d9">would be joined with</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-001</data>
