    <edge source="The Wardrobe" target="The Narrator">
      <data key="d7">8.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Narrator repeatedly visited The Wardrobe, the London residence of My Lord (Lord Sandwich), at various times and for a variety of purposes. On one occasion, the Narrator went there with Sir R. Slingsby and Slingsby’s brother. He also traveled to The Wardrobe after being at Westminster, sometimes going by water. During one visit he stayed a good while and spent the night in Mr. Moore’s chamber; on another day he went to The Wardrobe for dinner.

At other times, the Narrator supped at The Wardrobe with the ladies, where he heard that Lady Sandwich and the child were well. He also went there in the morning to take leave of Lord Hinchingbroke and the brother who was present. Additionally, he met his wife at The Wardrobe, dined there with the children, and visited his Lady. These visits reflect The Wardrobe as a central place for the Narrator’s social, familial, and service-related engagements with My Lord’s household.</data>
      <data key="d9">dine,go to,goes to,stayed at,supped,visit,visited,visits,water,went,went to,went_to</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-047</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1788445959</data>
