    <edge source="Mr. Moore" target="The Narrator">
      <data key="d7">8.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Mr. Moore and The Narrator were acquainted through a series of social, professional, and informational exchanges. The Narrator once stayed late at the Wardrobe and then went to bed with Mr. Moore in Mr. Moore's chamber. In a legal matter, Mr. Moore sent advice that the three witnesses being legatees would not harm the will. At Whitehall, Mr. Moore read over all the bills in The Narrator's presence, and he also told The Narrator there that Lady Sandwich had given birth to a daughter.

Socially, The Narrator found Mr. Moore at home and dined with him at an ordinary, took Mr. Moore to a tavern near the Savoy and drank with him, and walked with him into the City before they parted. Additionally, Mr. Moore had given The Narrator a handsomely bound copy of Hooker's Ecclesiastical Polity the previous Wednesday.</data>
      <data key="d9">advised,assisted,corresponded,dine with,drank with,find,gave,gifted,informed,news,parted,read over bills,slept in chamber,walked</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf47789c7f6b678113755e09e7199138-chunk-041</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1788445974</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
