    <edge source="My Lord" target="The Narrator">
      <data key="d7">5.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Narrator met My Lord at Whitehall, where My Lord stated that L300 must be laid out in cloth for presents in Barbary.&lt;SEP&gt;As The Narrator departed in the wherry, My Lord gave five guns, all they had charged, as a mark of great respect to The Narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;My Lord told The Narrator of his need for L300 laid out in cloth for presents in Barbary, at which The Narrator was glad.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator asked My Lord to order Mr. Creed to imprest money on The Narrator, with payment to be made by Alderman Backwell.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator stated to Lord Privy Seal that The Narrator had no deputation from My Lord.</data>
