    <edge source="The Diarist" target="My Lady">
      <data key="d7">8.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relationship between My Lady and The Diarist is shown through a series of personal visits and conversations, usually involving meals at My Lady’s residence, The Wardrobe. The Diarist sometimes came with My Wife; on one such visit, they dined with My Lady and were made much of. My Lady showed the greatest favour to The Diarist and his wife, and on another occasion The Diarist went to My Lady’s house and dined with her. One dinner at The Wardrobe took place while My Lady was in mourning.

During their meetings, matters were shared between them. The Diarist told My Lady about My Lord’s fortnight-long sickness and his recovery. My Lady also innocently told The Diarist about Mrs. Crispe’s intention concerning the King’s godfatherhood. Additionally, My Lady summoned The Diarist to stay and talk with her for about an hour. Overall, the records describe a cordial and hospitable connection between My Lady and The Diarist, with dining, mutual news, and extended conversation as recurring features.</data>
      <data key="d9">confided,conversed with,dined with,dines with,informed,showed favour,talked with,told,told news,visits</data>
